# Two languages: English and Myanmar

The site is bilingual. English (`en`) is at `/`, Myanmar (`my`) at `/my/`. Details: `docs/design/languages.md`.

## Always create both languages in the same task
- **Page:** markup in a shared view in `src/views/`, plus one route per locale (`src/pages/<path>.astro` and `src/pages/my/<path>.astro`).
- **UI text:** add the key to both `en` and `my` in `src/i18n/ui.ts`. Never hard-code visible text, `aria-label`, or SEO copy in components.
- Editing English interface copy means updating the Myanmar copy too, and the other way round.

## Articles
- One file: `src/content/articles/en/<slug>.md` or `src/content/articles/my/<slug>.md`. A matching file in the other folder is optional.
- The same file name links the language switcher when both files exist. Slugs stay English Latin letters.
- Authors publish from `/admin` (Sveltia CMS). Keep its fields in sync with `src/content.config.ts`.

## Myanmar quality
- Real Burmese in Unicode (not Zawgyi). Never leave English, placeholders, or "TODO: translate" in a `my` file.
- A Myanmar article is written in Burmese: title, description, headings, body, and image descriptions. When a second language file is added, keep the slug, dates, figures, and source URLs identical.
- First use of a medical term: Burmese, then the English term in brackets.
- Western digits for prices, dates, and figures.
- If you cannot translate something confidently, translate it as well as you can and tell the user which passages need a fluent reviewer.

## Links and locale
```astro
---
import { getLocale, localizePath, useTranslations } from '../i18n/ui';
const locale = getLocale(Astro.currentLocale);
const t = useTranslations(locale);
---
<!-- Good -->
<a href={localizePath(locale, '/articles/')}>{t('nav.articles')}</a>
<!-- Bad: hand-built prefix and hard-coded text -->
<a href="/my/articles/">Articles</a>
```
- Article URLs come from `getArticleUrl(article)`; dates from `formatDate(date, locale)`.
- Do not add a language fallback that shows English on a Myanmar URL.
